sue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"Ok, I want to use it from an installation directory, separate from my projects, so I won't get them contaminated.\r\n\r\nI have to run something like d:\\installdir\\psalm --init d:\\projectdir1\r\nit creates a psalm-xml file in the d:\\installdir\r\n\r\nWhen I want to check it, I run:\r\nd:\\installdir\\psalm --root=d:\\projectdir1\r\n(it was unclear where I should put that root statement, so I had to experiment.\r\n(could be changed in the documentation for clearness)\r\n\r\nAnyway: this goes wrong\r\nI have to move the creates config file to the d:\\projectdir1,\r\nchange the config into <directory name=\"\" />\r\nthen it runs.\r\n\r\nCan this be done simpler?\r\n\r\nand after a little while, I get this: Fatal error: Class 'Symfony\\Component\\ExpressionLanguage\\ExpressionLanguage' not found in d:\\installDir\\vendor\\symfony\\dependency-injection\\ExpressionLanguage.php on line 24\r\n\r\n\r\nBut, my original question is, what to do for the next project?\r\nbecause I now have to run something like d:\\installdir\\psalm --init d:\\projectdir2\r\nand here it complains, that the config file allready exists.\r\n\r\nI thinjk, the solution is, to create the psalm.xml in the target dir,\r\nor create a name that is not only spalm.xml, so the configuration file is per project.\r\n","closed_by":{"login":"muglug","id":2292638,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyOTI2Mzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2292638?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/muglug","html_url":"https://github.com/muglug","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muglug/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muglug/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muglug/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muglug/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muglug/subscriptions","